    'City of Dallas'::text,
    'City Council'::text,
    'Council member'::text,
    'Zarin Gracey'::text,
    'Zarin D. Gracey represents Dallas District 3. His background spans municipal budgeting, finance, procurement, business diversity, and economic development, as well as private-sector banking and finance. Before council service, he was District 3''s City Plan Commissioner and led the Dallas Public Facilities Corporation. He earned an accounting degree from the University of Arkansas at Pine Bluff, a master''s degree in organizational leadership from Luther Rice University and Seminary, and a state and local government credential from Harvard Kennedy School. His community involvement includes nonprofit boards and business organizations in Dallas.'::text,
    'https://dallascityhall.com/government/citycouncil/district3/Pages/default.aspx'::text,
