    'Council member'::text,
    'Jaime Resendez'::text,
    'Jaime Resendez represents Dallas District 5 and is listed as mayor pro tem in the city''s current council roster. A Pleasant Grove native, he served eight years as a U.S. Army engineer, including a deployment to Baghdad. He subsequently earned degrees from Eastfield Community College and the University of North Texas at Dallas and a law degree from the University of Texas. He was elected to the Dallas ISD board in 2016 and to the City Council in 2019. His official biography describes his work on schools in Pleasant Grove and identifies him as a practicing attorney.'::text,
    'https://dallascityhall.com/government/citycouncil/district5/Pages/council-member.aspx'::text,
