    'City of Dallas'::text,
    'City Council'::text,
    'Council member'::text,
    'Paul E. Ridley'::text,
    'Paul E. Ridley represents District 14 and first won the council seat in 2021. He holds a bachelor''s degree and master''s degrees in architecture and urban planning from the University of Michigan, and later earned a law degree at the University of Texas. His early career included municipal planning in Kansas City and architectural practice. In Dallas, he spent more than three decades working in construction law and commercial litigation and founded several law firms. Before joining the council, he represented District 14 on the City Plan Commission for eight years and the Landmark Commission for four years.'::text,
    'https://dallascityhall.com/government/citycouncil/district14/Pages/default.aspx'::text,
    'https://dallascityhall.com/government/citycouncil/district14/PublishingImages/Pages/default/PR%20HEADSHOT%2023.jpg'::text,
